    "body": "@mvdan\r\n> It's just perhaps less obvious to use a channel this way, if you conceptually think of the \"acquire semaphore\" operation as a \"get\".\r\n\r\nFWIW, you can modify the idiom somewhat to make it intuitive in the other direction: send-to-acquire is analogous to a “[lockout–tagout](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockout%E2%80%93tagout)” mechanism, where sending to the channel adds your lock and receiving from the channel removes it.",
